 "purpose": "Record shape for CORR4 section I sourceClass assignment provenance with physical evidence binding. One record per source-specific support record (fact x sourceRef); one computed segment per indivisible bounded segment. Enumerations are derived from boundaryModel (check S-7). The occurrence anchor block records the frame, the provisional occurrence, the anchor source, every failing condition and the unresolved reason (OA-12); the enumerations of frames, correspondence values and reasons are derived from boundaryModel (check S-7). The count block of an evaluation records, per count candidate, the B-2 basis-overlap diagnostics (basisOverlapRecord): component, members, overlap relations, support core, lawful-separation proofs and the count disposition; they are counting diagnostics, never states. The count block also records, for every non-overlapping pair of count candidates of one document, the touching-atom relation and its atom proof (touchingAtomRelation), and the SAME_INDIVISIBLE_ATOM_TOUCHING pairs with their lawful-separation proof (touchingAtomPair); they are counting diagnostics, never states. The SENTENCE evidence's continuation guard adds no field: a SENTENCE it does not prove rejects the record (SEPARATOR_EVIDENCE_FAILED) or leaves touching fragments to the touching-atom relation. A corpus may carry entityNameAuthority = {recordsSha256, records}: the frozen SEC entity-name authority candidate's records, read-only; the pilot replay names the RECORDS file by path and SHA-256. No segment-record field is added.",
